00:01:11.156 --> 00:01:14.316
Now, before we talk about AgentCore and best practices,

00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:21.836
let’s look at how an Agentic AI app differs from
any other normal application, which also uses generative AI.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.836
A lot of things. Andrew gave a very detailed presentation of Agentic.

00:01:27.316 --> 00:01:33.996
I'll summarize that in basically three traits
which an Agentic AI app has, which other apps don't.

00:01:34.436 --> 00:01:41.596
So the three primary differences. The first is that the Agentic AI
app tries to achieve an objective or a goal,

00:01:42.076 --> 00:01:48.676
and to achieve that objective or a goal, it takes a series of steps,
and the order of those steps is not always the same.

00:01:48.676 --> 00:01:50.916
So that's the first fundamental difference.

00:01:50.916 --> 00:01:57.876
The second difference is, since it takes a series of steps,
the whole interaction is long running or it is,

00:01:59.156 --> 00:02:06.076
you know, Stateful in nature. And hence the agent
needs to remember the context over a period of time,

00:02:06.076 --> 00:02:07.876
which can be hours or days sometimes.

00:02:07.876 --> 00:02:11.916
So this memory ability is the second fundamental difference.

00:02:11.996 --> 00:02:17.076
The third is in most of the scenarios,
the agent, in order to be helpful,

00:02:17.396 --> 00:02:21.436
have to integrate with multiple apps in the in the enterprise.

00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:25.476
And that it does by orchestrating
a series of tools which you give to it.

00:02:25.836 --> 00:02:28.956
So let's these three traits of an Agentic app.

00:02:28.956 --> 00:02:33.636
Let's keep them in mind because we'll
revisit them as we see the best practices.

00:02:34.076 --> 00:02:37.116
Now the brain of an Agentic AI app is still an LLM.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.516
It takes. It figures out what steps to take.

00:02:39.716 --> 00:02:46.676
It figures out which tools to call for which steps,
and then what to put in memory, when and when to read from memory.

00:02:47.836 --> 00:02:51.036
Now, when we are taking an Agentic AI app to production,

00:02:51.076 --> 00:02:55.756
we are faced with typical challenges
you are faced with for any other application, right?

00:02:55.756 --> 00:02:59.556
So we have to figure out how we'll host it, figure out how it will be.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:05.916
It will scale. You have to figure out how you'll secure it,
and you'll figure out how you will monitor or observe it.

00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:11.356
Now, these are all important concerns,
but it also constitutes undifferentiated heavy lifting.

00:03:11.716 --> 00:03:19.276
And this is where AgentCore helps us by eliminating all
these undifferentiated heavy lifting, by giving us ten capabilities.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:23.636
The first capability it gives us is an execution runtime.

00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:29.316
This execution runtime, you know,
so we can create an agent using any model or any framework,

00:03:29.316 --> 00:03:33.036
package it as a container, and AWS does the rest, right?

00:03:33.076 --> 00:03:42.436
So whether one user accesses it or 10,000 users accesses it,
the whole life cycle of the execution environment is managed by AWS.

00:03:43.676 --> 00:03:46.236
The second is how we talked about memory, right?

00:03:46.276 --> 00:03:48.316
So how does the agent get access to memory.

00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:54.156
It does it through AgentCore memory,
which is which provides the memory capability as a managed service.

00:03:54.156 --> 00:03:57.796
How does the agent talk to various tools in your enterprise.

00:03:57.796 --> 00:04:03.556
It does it through AgentCore Gateway, which allows it to access
various enterprise assets, whether they are Rest APIs,

00:04:03.556 --> 00:04:06.836
NCP servers, or or Lambda functions.

00:04:07.356 --> 00:04:10.636
Now, how all of this happens securely, right?

00:04:10.676 --> 00:04:16.516
How the how the agents are called securely,
how the agents call tools securely,

00:04:16.516 --> 00:04:22.316
how the tools call enterprise agents or enterprise
apps securely two legged authentication,

00:04:22.316 --> 00:04:27.716
three legged authentication or entry ID
all that is managed by AgentCore Identity.

